{
 "term": "2026-Fall",
 "course": "CS301 Automata",
 "name": "pda-parts",
 "title": "A pushdown automaton, part by part",
 "body": "<style>\n#fig text.label { font-size: 12.5px; }\n#fig .tex, #fig .tex-i { font-size: 12.5px; }\n@media (max-width: 600px) { #fig text.label { font-size: 20px; } #fig .tex, #fig .tex-i { font-size: 20px; } }\n</style>\n<header class=\"head\">\n<p class=\"tag\">[diagram, made by Mimir, simplified]</p>\n<h1>A pushdown automaton, part by part</h1>\n<p class=\"intro\">A PDA is a finite automaton with a stack. Click through to build one from its parts, shown partway through the PDA for \\(\\{a^{n}b^{n} \\mid n \\ge 0\\}\\) reading <span class=\"sym\">aabb</span>.</p>\n</header>\n<div class=\"board\" style=\"--sticky-fig: 20.5rem\">\n<figure>\n<svg id=\"fig\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 400\" role=\"img\">\n<title>Parts of a pushdown automaton</title>\n<desc>A sketch of a PDA partway through reading aabb. At the top, the input tape of four cells holding a, a, b, b, with a head pointing at the third cell, the first b. Below it the finite control, a box holding the states q0, q1, q2 and q3, with q3 drawn as an accepting double circle. Under the control the stack, a column of three cells holding X, X and $ from the top down. Beside the stack, the next move: b, X to epsilon. Labels: Input tape, Finite control, Stack, Moves.</desc>\n<rect class=\"ghost\" x=\"200\" y=\"80\" width=\"176\" height=\"44\"/>\n<rect class=\"ghost\" x=\"190\" y=\"190\" width=\"246\" height=\"80\"/>\n<rect class=\"ghost\" x=\"250\" y=\"300\" width=\"80\" height=\"90\"/>\n<g data-step=\"1\">\n<rect class=\"ink\" x=\"200\" y=\"80\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" fill=\"none\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n<rect class=\"ink\" x=\"244\" y=\"80\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" fill=\"none\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n<rect class=\"ink\" x=\"288\" y=\"80\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" fill=\"none\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n<rect class=\"ink\" x=\"332\" y=\"80\" width=\"44\" height=\"44\" fill=\"none\" pathLength=\"1\"/>\n<text class=\"tex\" x=\"222\" y=\"109\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text>\n<text class=\"tex\" x=\"266\" y=\"109\" text-anc