: in this course a PDA accepts by final state.</p></div>\n<div class=\"step\" data-step=\"3\"><div class=\"n\">3</div><p><span class=\"runin\">Stack:</span> only its top can be read, pushed or popped. $ marks the bottom; one X was pushed for each a read, so it holds X, X, $ from the top down.</p></div>\n<div class=\"step\" data-step=\"4\"><div class=\"n\">4</div><p><span class=\"runin\">Moves:</span> the control reads the symbol under the head and the top of the stack, then changes state, pops and pushes. The next move here reads b with X on top: \\(b, X \\to \\varepsilon\\), into \\(q_2\\).</p></div>\n<p class=\"caption caption-phone\" aria-hidden=\"true\">A sketch of the parts, not of a state diagram; the stack has no fixed height.</p>\n</div>\n</div>"
}
